  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Consider a linear transformation $\\,T\\,.$ If $\\,T({v}_{1}+3{v}_{2})=[\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,T({v}_{1})=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}]$, then find $\\,T({v}_{2}).$",
  "worked_solution": "Since $T$ is a linear transformation, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(v+kw)=T(v)+T(kw)=T(v)+kT(w)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor any vectors $v$ and $w.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T({v}_{1}+3{v}_{2}) & =T({v}_{1})+3T({v}_{2}) \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}]+3T({v}_{2}) \\\\ 3T({v}_{2}) & =[\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}] \\\\ 3T({v}_{2}) & =[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 18\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T({v}_{2}) & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 18\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T({v}_{2}) & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
